# State limits widened 2026-11-17 (modeled): the first armed Manual run on the 6X faulted a few ms after every (re)start, as the
# EKF2 attitude (about 10 ms period) makes the newest attitude sample routinely older than the newest gyro sample.
1	1	SLA_STATE_AGE	40	6
1	1	SLA_STATE_SKEW	25	6
1	1	SLA_MAN_WAIT	30	6
1	1	SLA_STATUS_AGE	1500000	6
1	1	SLA_ARM_AGE	800000	6
# Activation timing per mode (2026-11-10, modeled): flight banks poll every SLA_CYCLE_MIN, bench banks every 20 ms.
# Flight: first armed attempt on the 6X (2026-11-17): AUX replied in 4958 us, MAIN (PX4IO) not within 6500 us. Widened to
# 30000 / 20000 us with SLA_CYCLE_MAX 60000 (rules: ACK + FIRST_CMD < CYCLE_MAX, CYCLE_MIN < FIRST_CMD < CYCLE_MAX, reserve < OUT_LEASE).
# Measure the real reply times in 'slaaps status' (activation flight reply) and tighten; modeled until then.
# Bench: SLA_BN_* and SLA_BENCH_GAP 100 are the values that ran the servo bench on the Pixhawk 6X.
1	1	SLA_ACT_ACK_US	30000	6
1	1	SLA_FIRST_CMD_US	20000	6
1	1	SLA_BN_ACK_US	35000	6
1	1	SLA_BN_FIRST_US	40000	6
# 100 Hz (2026-11-17): at 4000 us the supervisor and both banks used about 54 percent of the CPU and starved the PX4IO queue (idle 2.6 percent,
# MAIN activation intermittently late). 10000 us halved the supervisor load and left 12.5 percent idle; EKF2 attitude arrives at about 100 Hz anyway.
1	1	SLA_CYCLE_MIN	10000	6
1	1	SLA_CYCLE_MAX	60000	6
1	1	SLA_BENCH_GAP	100	6
1	1	SLA_OUT_LEASE	100	6
